      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:3:103:2",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لَهُ الرَّجُلُ يَتَزَوَّجُ مُتْعَةً سَنَةً أَوْ أَقَلَّ أَوْ أَكْثَرَ قَالَ إِذَا كَانَ شَيْئاً مَعْلُوماً إِلَى أَجَلٍ مَعْلُومٍ قَالَ قُلْتُ وَ تَبِينُ بِغَيْرِ طَلَاقٍ قَالَ نَعَمْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Ismail, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan Al-Reza<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I said to him<sup>asws</sup>, ‘The man marries by <span class=\"iTxt\">Mut’a</span> for a year, or less or more’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When it was a known thing to a known term’. I said, ‘And she would be irrevocably divorced without a (formal) divorce?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn ‘Isma’il who has said the following: “In response to my question before al-Rida’, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a man who marries in the manner of al-Mut‘ah (advantageous marriage) for one year or less or more, he (the Imam) said, ‘It is permissible if it is a known matter for a known number of days.’ I then asked if it terminates without divorce. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, it terminates without divorce.”’ "
        ]
      }
